HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The sseenndd() function appeared in 4.2BSD.  The sseennddmmmmssgg() function appeared
     in FreeBSD 11.0.

BBUUGGSS
     Because sseennddmmssgg() does not necessarily block until the data has been
     transferred, it is possible to transfer an open file descriptor across an
     AF_UNIX domain socket (see recv(2)), then cclloossee() it before it has actu‐
     ally been sent, the result being that the receiver gets a closed file de‐
     scriptor.  It is left to the application to implement an acknowledgment
     mechanism to prevent this from happening.

